  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Modern Technology Solutions received $436M in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Modern Technology Solutions recorded 49 awards so far in the fiscal year, with an average award size of $8.9M. Modern Technology Solutions saw obligations up 10.2% year over year. Modern Technology Solutions has grown obligations each multi-year snapshot from $137M in FY21 to $436M in FY26, with a peak at $396M in FY25 before the current-year total. Modern Technology Solutions sells primarily research and development services, including $252M in Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Biotechnology) and $117M in Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology). Modern Technology Solutions also provides Engineering Services, which totaled $41.5M, and Custom Computer Programming Services, which totaled $7.4M. Modern Technology Solutions takes most of its FY2026 business from the General Services Administration, which obligated $264M, followed by the Department of Defense, which obligated $166M, and the Department of Homeland Security, which obligated $6.3M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies are buying from Modern Technology Solutions?",
        "body": "General Services Administration is the largest buyer, with $264M in obligations in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense follows with $166M in obligations. The Department of Homeland Security has $6.3M in obligations."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are Modern Technology Solutions' primary market areas?",
        "body": "Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Biotechnology) is the largest market with $252M in FY2026 to date. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) accounts for $117M. Engineering Services accounts for $41.5M, with smaller shares in Custom Computer Programming Services at $7.4M and Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing at $5.1M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Modern Technology Solutions make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Modern Technology Solutions makes $436M from federal contracts in FY2026 to date. Modern Technology Solutions recorded 49 awards so far this fiscal year and an average award size of $8.9M, and obligations are up 10.2% year over year. Historical obligations by fiscal year were $137M in FY21, $172M in FY22, $251M in FY23, $226M in FY24, and $396M in FY25."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Modern Technology Solutions?",
      "a": "General Services Administration buys the most from Modern Technology Solutions, obligating $264M in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense is the next largest buyer with $166M in obligations, followed by the Department of Homeland Security at $6.3M."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Modern Technology Solutions sell to the government?",
      "a": "Modern Technology Solutions sells research and development and engineering services to the government. Modern Technology Solutions reported $252M in Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Biotechnology), $117M in Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology), $41.5M in Engineering Services, and $7.4M in Custom Computer Programming Services."
